"[2512.07369] Alperin's weight conjecture, Galois automorphisms, alternating sums, and functorial equivalences (https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.07369)\nciteturn1view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.07369\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 159\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Representation Theory\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 8 Dec 2025]\nL9: # Title:Alperin's weight conjecture, Galois automorphisms, alternating sums, and functorial equivalences\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Xin Huang , cite6†Deniz Yılmaz L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Alperin's weight conjecture, Galois automorphisms, alternating sums, and functorial equivalences, by Xin Huang and 1 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite7†View PDF cite8†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:We show that functorial equivalences can offer new insight into the blockwise Galois Alperin weight conjecture (BGAWC). Inspired by Knörr and Robinson's work, we first formulate the BGAWC in terms of alternating sums indexed by chains of $p$-subgroups, and we also give a functorial reformulation in the Grothendieck group of diagonal $p$-permutation functors. We prove that these formulations are equivalent.\nL17: We further show that if a functorial equivalence between a block with abelian defect group and its Brauer correspondent descends to the minimal field of the block, then the BGAWC holds for that block. Finally, we prove that Galois conjugate blocks are functorially equivalent over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero.\nL18: Subjects:  | Representation Theory (math.RT); Group Theory (math.GR)\nL19: Cite as:  | cite9†arXiv:2512.07369 [math.RT]\nL20:    | (or cite10†arXiv:2512.07369v1 [math