 for simple groups. We proceed in two steps to refine this reduction. First, we propose the blockwise Galois Alperin weight (BGAW) conjecture and define its associated inductive BGAW condition.\nL17: Second, assuming the inductive GAW (respectively, BGAW) condition for simple groups, we establish a stronger version of the GAW (respectively, BGAW) conjecture in terms of central (respectively, block) isomorphism of H-triples.\nL18: Comments:  | 37 pages\nL19: Subjects:  | Group Theory (math.GR)\nL20: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 20C20\nL21: Cite as:  | cite11†arXiv:2512.15243 [math.GR]\nL22:    | (or cite12†arXiv:2512.15243v2 [math.GR] for this version)\nL23:    | cite13†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2512.15243†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Qulei Fu [cite14†view email ]\nL27: cite5†[v1] Wed, 17 Dec 2025 09:43:14 UTC (39 KB)\nL28: [v2] Fri, 24 Apr 2026 06:06:05 UTC (39 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled A reduction theorem for the blockwise Navarro Alperin weight conjecture via H-triples, by Zhicheng Feng and 2 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * cite9†View PDF L37:   * cite10†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite15†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite16†view license L41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: math.GR\nL44: \nL45: cite17†< prev |   cite18†next > L46: \nL47: cite19†new | cite20†recent | cite21†2025-12 L48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: cite22†math L52: \nL53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * cite23†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L56:   * cite24†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L57:   * cite25†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L58: \nL59: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL60: \nL61: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL62: \nL63: [Button: ×]\nL64: \nL65: loading...\nL66: \nL67: Data provided by:\nL68: \nL69: ### Bookmark\nL70: \nL