cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Representation Theory\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 7 Apr 2026 (cite5†v1 ), last revised 7 May 2026 (this version, v3)]\nL9: # Title:The Galois Alperin weight conjecture for finite category algebras\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Xin Huang L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled The Galois Alperin weight conjecture for finite category algebras, by Xin Huang\nL14: \nL15: cite7†View PDF cite8†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Let $p$ be a prime, $k$ an algebraic closure of $\\mathbb{F}_p$ and $\\Gamma$ the Galois group ${\\rm Gal}(k/\\mathbb{F}_p)$. Let $\\mathcal{C}$ be a finite category and $\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}}$ the $p$-orbit category of $\\mathcal{C}$ defined by Linckelmann.\nL17: We formulate a version of the Galois Alperin weight conjecture (GAWC) for finite category algebras stating that there exists a $\\Gamma\\times {\\rm Aut}(\\mathcal{C})$-equivariant bijection between the set of isomorphism classes of simple $k\\mathcal{C}$-modules and that of the weights of $k\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}}$. We reduce the GAWC for finite categories to finite groups.\nL18: For $\\mathcal{C}$ an EI-category, we give a partition of weights of $k\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}}$ with respect to blocks of $k\\mathcal{C}$ and then formulate a blockwise Galois Alperin weight conjecture (BGAWC) for $\\mathcal{C}$. Similarly, we reduce the BGAWC for finite EI-categories to finite groups.\nL19: Subjects:  | Representation Theory (math.RT); Group Theory (math.GR)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite9†arXiv:2604.06166 [math.RT]\nL21:    | (or cite10†arXiv:2604.06166v3 [math.RT] for this version)\nL22:    | cite11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2604.06166†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Xin Huang [cite12†view email ]\nL26: cite5†[v1] Tue, 7 Apr 2026 17:58:57 UTC (15 KB)\nL27: cite13†[v2] Mon, 4 May 2026 16:05:32 UTC (27 KB)\nL28: [v3] Thu, 7 May 2026 17:55:10 UTC (28 KB)\