s†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL159: cite45†About†info.arxiv.org · cite46†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite47†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite48†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite49†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite50†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite51†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite52†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L160: \nL161: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2507.20314] On Alperin's conjecture and functorial equivalence of blocks (https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.20314)\nciteturn1view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.20314\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 161\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Representation Theory\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 27 Jul 2025]\nL9: # Title:On Alperin's conjecture and functorial equivalence of blocks\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Robert Boltje , cite6†Serge Bouc , cite7†Deniz Yılmaz L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled On Alperin's conjecture and functorial equivalence of blocks, by Robert Boltje and 2 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of positive characteristic $p$ and let $\\mathbb{F}$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic 0. We consider Alperin's weight conjecture (over $k$) from the point of view of (stable) functorial equivalence of blocks over $\\mathbb{F}$. We formulate a functorial version of Alperin's blockwise weight conjecture, and show that it is equivalent to the original one.\nL17: We also show that this conjecture holds stably, i.e., in the category of stable diagonal $p$-permutation functors over $\\mathbb{F}$.\nL18: Comments:  | 10 pages\nL19: Subjects:  | Representation Theory (math.RT); Group Theory (math.GR)\nL20: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 20C20 (Primary) 20J15, 19A22 (Secondary)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:2507.20314 [math.RT]\nL22:    | (or cite11†arXiv:2507.20314v1 [math.RT] for this version)\nL23:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2507.20314†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Robert Boltje [cite13†view email ]\nL27: [v1] Sun, 27 Jul 2025 15:10:54 UTC (13 KB)\nL28: \nL29: Full-text links:\nL30: \nL31: ## Access Paper:\nL32: \nL33: View a PDF of the paper titled On Alperin's conjecture and functorial equivalence of blocks, by Robert Boltje and 2 other authors\nL34: \nL35:   * cite8†View PDF L36:   * cite9†HTML (experimental) L37:   * cite14†TeX Source L38: \nL39: cite15†view license L40: \nL41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: math.RT\nL44: \nL45: cite16†< prev |   cite17†next > L46: \nL47: cite18†new | cite19†recent | cite20†2025-07 L48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: cite21†math L52: cite22†math.GR L53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * cite23†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L56:   * cite24†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L57:   * cite25†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L58: \nL59: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL60: \nL61: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL62: \nL63: [Button: ×]\nL64: \nL65: loading...\nL66: \nL67: Data provided by:\nL68: \nL69: ### Bookmark\nL70: \nL71: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL72: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL73: \nL74: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL75: \nL76: Bibliographic Explorer (cite26†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL77: \nL78: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL79: \nL80: Connected Papers (cite27†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpapers.com )\nL81: \nL82: [Input] Litma